\n$$\ny=-x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-2t}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line and approach the origin as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=-x$ is $\\text{a stable}$ line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{a saddle point}.$ \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069584/assets/a09d50fa36b2748fb1c65ed16e20d950afbbabc18884ff8718cf1571c4e13b0e.png)" 13194139535698 true] [17592186362034 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362035 13194139535698 true] [17592186362034 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362036 13194139535698 true] [17592186362034 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362037 13194139535698 true] [17592186362034 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362038 13194139535698 true] [17592186362034 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535698 true] [17592186362034 1041 "field-1" 13194139535698 true] [17592186362034 1104 #edb/ref 17592186362036 13194139535698 true] [17592186362034 1110 #uuid "4f7ce5e4-7521-5ffb-9069-e71f9c759086" 13194139535698 true] [17592186362035 1034 "y=2x" 13194139535698 true] [17592186362035 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535698 true] [17592186362035 1111 #uuid "4c77329a-553b-5136-90ca-3332a11fab58" 13194139535698 true] [17592186362036 1034 "y=x" 13194139535698 true] [17592186362036 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535698 true] [17592186362036 1111 #uuid "bbdc1dd6-0ea9-5d8f-a55b-1af1493d2930" 13194139535698 true] [17592186362037 1034 "y=-2x" 13194139535698 true] [17592186362037 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535698 true] [17592186362037 1111 #uuid "acee8661-656a-51fd-9bb1-8e8884a321cc" 13194139535698 true] [17592186362038 1034 "y=-x" 13194139535698 true] [17592186362038 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535698 true] [17592186362038 1111 #uuid "207969c7-e8e4-5674-a8e6-a21b13b2ff53" 13194139535698 true] [17592186362039 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362040 13194139535698 true] [17592186362039 100