 R.\n$$\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{2t}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line and approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $y=-\\frac{1}{2}x$ is $\\text{an unstable}$ line.\n\n- The line that passes through the origin and is parallel to ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ has the equation \n\n$$\nx=0.\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on that line and approach infinity as $t\\to \\infty .$ So, $x=0$ is $\\text{an unstable}$ line.\n\nTherefore, the equilibrium point (origin) is $\\text{an unstable node (source)}.$ \n\n**Note:** The phase portrait of the system looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069584/assets/0d9e032bfffa68f487347d6c169999e313247e89ef7de3fae28edb216dcf718f.png)" 13194139535698 true] [17592186362050 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362051 13194139535698 true] [17592186362050 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362052 13194139535698 true] [17592186362050 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535698 true] [17592186362050 1041 "field-1" 13194139535698 true] [17592186362050 1104 #edb/ref 17592186362052 13194139535698 true] [17592186362050 1110 #uuid "404e91c1-8a4b-529d-a64a-d5a197f1d3fb" 13194139535698 true] [17592186362051 1034 "a stable" 13194139535698 true] [17592186362051 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535698 true] [17592186362051 1111 #uuid "59f9777e-4b3c-50f8-a5e6-78ff3a79c58f" 13194139535698 true] [17592186362052 1034 "an unstable" 13194139535698 true] [17592186362052 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535698 true] [17592186362052 1111 #uuid "f2a6b7e3-ff52-56d9-8c93-ce1126b6d864" 13194139535698 true] [17592186362053 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362054 13194139535698 true] [175921863620